Feature: Insert new region record into config_master table

  Background:
    Given the {{config_master}} table exists in the Unity Catalog purgo_playground

  Scenario: Retrieve and modify existing record for new region
    Given a record exists in the {{config_master}} table with src_objt_name "Sales"
    When I retrieve the record
    Then I modify the record with the following values
      | src_objt_name          | ID_Sales                         |
      | src_sys                | ID_Sales                         |
      | f_format               | ID_MON_Sales_                    |
      | s3_landing_path        | s3a://{s3_bucket}/landing/ID/ID_Sales/ |
      | s3_archive_path        | s3a://{s3_bucket}/archive/ID/ID_Sales/ |
      | country                | ID                               |
      | region                 | ID                               |
      | affiliate_group        | ID                               |
      | affiliate              | ID                               |
      | src_layer              | ID_Sales                         |
      | target_src_sys         | ID_Sales                         |
      | delta_stg_tables       | stg_ID_sales                     |
      | source_path            | /SecureFtp/-InternalX/ID/IN/DATA/Sales/ |
      | actual_file_name       | {"ID_MON_Sales_*": "stg_ID_wholesaler"} |
      | dag_id                 | LOAD_SALES_ID                    |
    Then I append the modified record back to the {{config_master}} table

  Scenario Outline: Validate error conditions and insertion
    Given the following values are being inserted
      | src_objt_name  | ID_Sales        |
      | src_sys        | ID_Sales        |
      | s3_landing_path| <landing_path>  |
      | s3_archive_path| <archive_path>  |
    When I validate these values
    Then "<expected_message>" should be returned

    Examples:
      | landing_path                        | archive_path                        | expected_message                    |
      | s3a://{{s3_bucket}}/landing/ID/ID_Sales/ | s3a://{{s3_bucket}}/archive/ID/ID_Sales/ | Success                             |
      | invalid_path                        | s3a://{{s3_bucket}}/archive/ID/ID_Sales/ | Error: Invalid Landing Path        |
      | s3a://{{s3_bucket}}/landing/ID/ID_Sales/ | invalid_path                        | Error: Invalid Archive Path        |

  Scenario: Confirm column updates and dependencies
    Given the config_id column is unique
    When a new record is added
    Then ensure no other column is updated incorrectly

  Scenario: Validate integrity and archival strategy
    Given a historical data integrity requirement
    When a new record is added
    Then ensure previous records are archived properly

  Scenario: Validate constraints before insertion
    Given data validation constraints are applied
    When inserting modified values into {{config_master}}
    Then integrity checks for src_objt_name and src_sys are performed

  Scenario: Validate logging and error reporting
    Given logging is enabled for operations
    When an insertion error occurs
    Then an error message with a tracking ID is logged

  Scenario Outline: Comprehensive operational validation
    Given a new record is prepared for insertion
    When inserting data with <validation_type>
    Then <result> should be confirmed

    Examples:
      | validation_type | result   |
      | Integrity       | Pass     |
      | Validation      | Pass     |
      | Logging         | Success  |
